In article <1171@devnull.mpd.tandem.com> dwelch@devnull.mpd.tandem.com (Dan Welch) writes:
>I was just playing, wishing for a potion of gain ability, when it
>suddenly struck me that there is no analogy for a magic marker as
>far as potions go.
>
>How about introducing a "magic tap", that can spew forth any potion
>that you've already identified?  Maybe it wouldn't be something you
>can carry around, but would be fixed like a sink or a fountain.  In
>addition, there could be empty bottles, similar in idea to a blank
>scroll.  To keep people from getting a dozen gain ability potions,
>there could be no way to empty a bottle, though you can erase a scroll.

Why not have it so that when you quaff from a sink and have a potion
spew forth, that if you have an empty bottle, the game asks you

Fill your bottle (y/n)

and you can then decide whether or not you want that type of potion.

This would only occur if you have an empty bottle and would only fill
one bottle.

Alternately, it would only occur if you also have a bottling kit,
analogous to the tinning kit.  Maybe this would allow you to bottle
water from fountains?

